"Primary Caxri Capability" means a user-facing or programmable capability that is material to Caxri
as distributed, including Projects, Sessions, Agent Chat, the Terminal, Files, Source Control, the
Server, and the CLI, and any substitute that supplies substantially the same function to another
person.

"Hosted Access" means allowing another person to use a Primary Caxri Capability over a network,
